-- 20260716_cbam_default_values_seed.sql
-- Seed for public.cbam_default_values — IR 2025/2621 Annex I, "Other Countries and Territories"
-- fallback defaults for iron & steel (the country-agnostic fallback used when no country-specific
-- default applies). country = 'other' for every row.
-- Inserts the 200 numeric rows of the iron & steel section only.
-- The section's 21 "see below" heading rows are DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED: 7206, 7207, 7211, 7214, 7217,
-- 7218, 7219, 7220, 7222, 7223, 7224, 7225, 7226, 7228, 7303, 7304, 7306, 7307, 7311, 7318, 7326.
-- They carry "see below" in all six value columns — navigation pointers, not values — and resolve to
-- their 8-digit children at lookup time. Seeding them would assert a figure the source does not give.
-- description seeded NULL for every row: labels are deferred to the authoritative CN nomenclature,
-- keyed by cn_code, rather than taken from the 2621 PDF extract (kerning artifacts; the extract reads
-- "polygamol" for "polygonal" at 7224 90 90). Numeric columns and CN codes are the verified data.
-- All values transcribed verbatim; decimal comma -> decimal point is the only change. Nothing recomputed:
-- see_total is transcribed as printed even where it != see_direct + see_indirect (2601 12 00 sintered ore
-- prints 0.686 against a 0.687 sum — source rounding, preserved).
-- see_indirect is NULL where the source prints N/A (199 of 200 rows); sintered ore 2601 12 00 is the only
-- row in the section carrying a real indirect value. NULL means "not given", never 0.
-- Mark-up columns are the source's own printed figures (10/20/30% on TOTAL), not derived here.
-- cbam_bm_route verbatim, including the five compound '(C)/(F)' values (7227, 7228 30, 7228 50, 7229,
-- 7304 59); NULL where the source prints no indicator.

